  "adaptation": {
    "nativeInput": "Existing public control.Slider, RangeSlider and SliderValues. Actual RoleSlider thumbs own native focus, keyboard, pointer capture and AX ranges. No fake visual-only controls.",
    "defaults": "Docs demo/RTL75, Create Basic50, disabled50; range25/50 step5; multiple10/20/70 step10; vertical pair50/25 max100 step1; controlled0.3/0.7 min0 max1 step0.1. All recipe drafts independent.",
    "sourceLayout": "Docs max-w-xs320DIP. Create unspecified width fills the native card. Vertical pair h-40=160DIP and gap-6=24DIP, centered docs row; Create keeps intrinsic centered pair. Controlled gap-3=12DIP and label/readout gap-2=8DIP.",
    "label": "Bare source sliders have no supplied visible label. Native-only accessible Slider/Vertical slider 1/Vertical slider 2 names are added; controlled retains the visible Temperature label and grouped native LabelledBy.",
    "readout": "Source joined decimal readout updates from the application values. Native binary fractional step noise is rounded to the declared tenth for display only; stored numeric values remain unchanged.",
    "rtl": "Source translations have empty value dictionaries; the language selector changes direction without inventing translated visible labels. Arabic default, Hebrew and English retain native horizontal geometry; vertical stays bottom-to-top.",
    "localBehavior": "Only numeric draft changes and diagnostic counters. No invented submit/save/network behavior or action status for source examples without handlers.",
    "lifecycle": "Application only stores values, strings, booleans and counts; no Context, Element, FieldScope or frame callback. Configuration/language selector uses Gallery Flyout or OS menu mode.",
    "verification": "One public native-input flow and four representative software PNGs. Injected selector Backend does not establish real OS tracking, assistive technology, IME, fonts or complete platform/visual matrices.",
    "disabledStyle": "The source Control supplies the single data-disabled opacity-50 layer. BaseUI visible Thumb is a div; its disabled:opacity-50 pseudo-class does not match, while its hidden input is disabled. Native explicit Disabled root uses one half-opacity layer and native thumbs disable input without another dim. Ancestor-only disabled remains one inherited layer."
  },
